# Code clarity

- **Readers first**: if a name needs a comment to understand, **rename** instead.
- **Comments**: explain **why** (constraints, quirks, trade-offs) and, when the mechanics stay opaque, **what/how in plain language** — see [human-comments.mdc](./human-comments.mdc) (regex, backoff, workarounds).
- Do **not** narrate obvious lines (`// set x to 1`).
- **One level of abstraction per function**: if you can name a block with a phrase, extract a well-named private method.
- **HTTP layer**: status codes and error shapes should be obvious from the method that sends them (e.g. `sendBadRequestForInvalidContext`).

**Before finishing:** did we avoid abbreviations except industry-standard ones (`id`, `url`, `http`)? Are comments only where clarity would otherwise be lost?
